Finally, some twenty years after trying Nethack for the first time I
have managed to ascend with my first character.

Balstyrko's story:
Right from the start things seemed to be going well for Balstyrko. Of
course being a Valkyrie the first levels are pretty easy just bashing
the monsters. After that it was trivial to dip for Excalibur. Once the
mines and sokoban was finished she headed to a Lawful altar on level
12. A blessed scroll of identify revealed 3 scrolls of Genocide in her
inventory. After blessing those I got rid of all 'L' and ';'. I wanted
to also kill off all minflayers but fortunately the spoilers warned me
against doing a genocide on 'h' when playing as a dwarf. Also in the
inventory was a Wand of Charging, which saved a wish at the Castle.
Some poly-piling at this time also produced 6 potions of Gain Level
which were saved for later in the game to boost her level from 20 to
26 before making the run up through the dungeon with the amulet.

After dealing with the Castle and wishing for the items needed in a
good ascension kit it was pretty much straight forward until the end
except from a few unfortunate incidents:
- Running into a Mindflayer a lot of object identification information
disappeared, I really _hate_ this monster.
- After killing the Moloch high priest in the final level with a
cocatrice corpse Balstyrko managed to fall into a pit carrying the
corpse. Only an amulet of Lifesaving spared the embarrasment of YASD.

My own story with Nethack:
I first tried Nethack in 1987 or 1989 after getting it on a floppy
disk from a friend. This was the good old DOS days when you had to add
a reference to "ansi.sys" in the config.sys.

At that time there was no Internet to provide spoilers or even tell
you how to win the game so it was just a merry hack and slash game. I
played it a bit on and off over the years until about six years ago
when I started reading lots of spoilers and tried seriously to do an
ascension. It didn't happen though and Nethack was put aside until two
weeks ago when I started playing again and this time, with massive
help from the spoilers, I managed to ascend with my first character.


